  "digest": "# INDUSTRIALS \u2014 2026-W45 (week to 2026-11-07)\n\n## Coverage changes\nFive updates published on 5-Nov; a sixth is held. [ASII](coverage/companies/ASII.JK/report.md) moved ADD\u2192**HOLD 4,712** (was 4,849; TR +9.2%) on the LCGC release and a correction of our own parent-cover statement. [TOBA](coverage/companies/TOBA.JK/report.md) moved SELL\u2192**HOLD 395** (was 304; TR +7.2%) after removing a waste-EBITDA double count and marking waste on the disclosed nine-month figure. [ABMM](coverage/companies/ABMM.JK/report.md) stays **ADD 2,621** (was 2,764) on a rebuilt SOTP using 30-Sep net debt. [DSSA](coverage/companies/DSSA.JK/report.md) stays **SELL 441** (was 488; TR \u221229.5%): OJK restitution enters the governance file, not the base case. [FOLK](coverage/companies/FOLK.JK/report.md) stays **SELL 26** (was 23; TR \u221255%). [BRPT](coverage/companies/BRPT.JK/report.md)'s rewrite to REDUCE 803 is parked pending BREN's Sector Lead sign-off, so its published record remains HOLD 1,111. Heavy equipment, industrial goods and services still have no published name; 62 initiations are queued.\n\n## Deck moves\nNo INDUSTRIALS-owned deck moved. The konglo regime scalars are unchanged at 30% base gap compression and 25/50/25 scenario weights [deck konglo S1\u2013S5]. The coal deck's spot of US$150.35/t (15-Oct) still sits 27.4% above its FY2027E US$118 [deck coal S19]; that is the live input behind DSSA's and CUAN's coal marks.\n\n## Material news\nOJK is calculating investor restitution for the DSSA/BREN/CUAN share case but named no amount, timing or payer (CNBC, 5-Nov); HSC names left the IHSG calculation on 2-Nov and OJK has not filed criminal charges (CNBC, 2-Nov). ASII's LCGC wholesales fell 11% in 9M-2026 while the national market grew 21%, with trade-up and cheap EVs cited (Okezone, 4-Nov). TOBA's waste revenue rose 41% in 9M with Rp7.77tn of investment pending (Kontan, 2-Nov). FOLK fell 24% over five days (78\u219259, 31-Oct to 6-Nov); the 4-Nov release shows cash against liabilities after portfolio sales and a >5% holder sold again on 3-Nov, so the move is not fully attributable.\n\n## What to watch\nASII: 10-Nov October GAIKINDO wholesales and the 11-Nov Otoparts tender close. DSSA: restitution mechanics and the HSC methodology review. BRPT: BREN sign-off, then re-publication. TOBA: whether the disclosed nine-month waste run-rate holds. FOLK: surveillance and further holder selling.\n\nResearch only; not investment advice.",
